      "options": {
        "content": "Use `trace_id` from a Document completion log to open the matching Tempo trace. Split results by the fixed `generate_document` and `find_documents` operations, then correlate render with JSReport, upload/object lookup with object storage, and metadata/metadata lookup with PostgreSQL. A rendered document is not yet stored; a stored object is not yet registered; only a successful owned lookup proves retrievability. Inspect the fixed `registered` worker outcome, duration, commit-failure and in-flight signals. Legitimate idle time has zero request/event rates, present Go runtime samples, enabled state matching configuration and zero in-flight age. Disabled mode reports enabled zero. Silence does not prove caught-up state or completeness. An available deployment without a runtime sample is missing telemetry; rising shared drop, failure, lag or queue signals indicate collection failure. Labels remain bounded and never expose policy/customer data, PDF bytes, object keys, event bodies, topics, groups, credentials, arbitrary errors or trace IDs.",
